rity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Logan, CO; Phillips, CO; Sedgwick, CO; Washington, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b5fc3fb0f4468acf2c3b7dde0584271abf13df82.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b5fc3fb0f4468acf2c3b7dde0584271abf13df82.001.1"},{"event":"Severe Thunderstorm Watch","headline":"Severe Thunderstorm Watch issued August 15 at 6:49PM MDT until August 15 at 9:00PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"SEVERE THUNDERSTORM WATCH 584 REMAINS VALID UNTIL 9 PM MDT THIS\nEVENING FOR THE FOLLOWING AREAS\n\nIN COLORADO THIS WATCH INCLUDES 3 COUNTIES\n\nIN EAST CENTRAL COLORADO\n\nLINCOLN\n\nIN NORTHEAST COLORADO\n\nLOGAN                 WASHINGTON\n\nTHIS INCLUDES THE CITIES OF AKRON, LIMON, AND STERLING.","ends":"2026-08-15T21:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Lincoln, CO; Logan, CO; Washington, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b88c55a0c3796e766715719127486f7ebcc20d9c.002.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b88c55a0c3796e766715719127486f7ebcc20d9c.002.1"},{"event":"Flood Advisory","headline":"Flood Advisory issued August 15 at 5:31PM MDT until August 15 at 8:30PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Southeastern Logan County in northeastern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 830 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\nRises in small streams and normally dry creeks.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n\n- At 530 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to\nthunderstorms. Minor flooding is ongoing or expected to begin\nshortly in the advisory area. Up to 0.5 inches of rain have\nfallen.\n\n- Additional rainfall amounts of 0.5 to 1.5 inches are expected\nover the area. This additional rain will result in minor\nflooding.\n\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nSterling, Fleming, Iliff, St Petersburg, Proctor, Padroni,\nAtwood, Reiradon Hill and Dailey.","ends":"2026-08-15T20:30:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Logan, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.756e9c2e82a8d04ed7b54dd61b6f3fea90953de9.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.756e9c2e82a8d04ed7b54dd61b6f3fea90953de9.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued August 15 at 11:32AM MDT until August 16 at 6:00AM MDT by NWS Goodland KS","description":"* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall is possible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of east central Colorado, including the following\narea, Cheyenne CO and west central Kansas, including the following\nareas, Gove, Greeley, Logan, Wallace and Wichita.\n\n* WHEN...From 6 PM MDT  /7 PM CDT/ this evening through late tonight.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nLow-water crossings may be flooded.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- 1-3 inches of rain the past couple nights along with the\npotential for another cluster or two of storms this evening and\novernight increases the potential for some flooding and even\nflash flooding. Rainfall rates of 1.5 to 2.5 inches per hour is\npossible in the strongest cells.","ends":"2026-08-16T06:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Cheyenne County; Wallace; Logan; Gove; Greeley; Wichita","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e088e0765aa75bc050e847f792689803d87d9b3f.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e088e0765aa75bc050e847f792689803d87d9b3f.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-08-15T23:41:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 152341 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 541 PM MDT Sat Aug 15 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Thunderstorms capable of producing heavy rainfall and flash flooding continue through Sunday with a few strong to severe thunderstorms across the southeast plains both days. - Thunderstorm activity a little less widespread for Monday as drier air works in from the","url":"https://forecast.we